-- | Ipe.Env — build-time-embedded public config.
--
-- `Env.public "KEY"` reads a value baked into the compiled artifact at BUILD
-- time, not the live process environment. It resolves ONLY for a name on the
-- project's `[wasm] publicEnv` allowlist (`package.ipe`), which is itself
-- validated against a secret-name denylist (any `_`-delimited component that
-- is a secret word — `SECRET` / `TOKEN` / `KEY` / `PASSWORD` / `PASSWD` /
-- `CREDENTIAL` / `AUTH` / `APIKEY` — plus `DATABASE_URL` and the `IPE_*`
-- namespace), the temp-root and home names (`TMPDIR` / `TMP` / `TEMP` /
-- `HOME` / `USERPROFILE` / `HOMEDRIVE` / `HOMEPATH`, any case), the portable
-- name grammar, and repeats at manifest PARSE time — allowlisting a refused
-- name is a build error, never a runtime refusal. Any key not on the allowlist returns `Nothing`; there is
-- no way to reach the raw host/process environment through this function on
-- either target.
--
-- Use case: a browser bundle (`--target wasm`) has no live process
-- environment to call `System.getenv` against — this is the narrow,
-- allowlisted substitute. Works identically on the native target too (same
-- allowlist, read via the live environment there) so a `view`/config module
-- shared between a native SSR path and a wasm client type-checks — and
-- behaves identically — against both.
--
-- `System.getenv` stays a DOES-NOT-exist-for-wasm kernel regardless: public
-- build-time config is a distinct, narrower surface, never a `getenv`
-- backdoor.
module Ipe.Env exposing
    ( public
    )

import Ipe.Ffi.Kernel as Kernel


-- | `public key` — the build-time-embedded value for `key`, or `Nothing`
-- when `key` is not on this project's `[wasm] publicEnv` allowlist.
public : String -> Maybe String
public =
    Kernel.kernel "Env_public"
